            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_11",
            "review_title": "Review at Be Anh Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Robert K\nSingapore, null, Singapore2 contributions\n2\nGot cheated big time\nAug 2019\nThe restaurant was recommended by the hotel receptionist. When we took the taxi, the driver using a translator tried to get me to go to a different restaurant saying that Be Anh is VERY EXPENSIVE. We had a small 600 grams crab, two cray fish and a squid. We ordered two small coconuts. The food was so so and the service was bad but the restaurant was pretty crowded with locals. \n\nWe ordered Chinese spinach but it did not come and so we canceled it. The squid was tough and we just chew and spit it out. The crayfish had very ltille meat on them. By vetry little it was like less that a small teaspoonful for meat.\n\nWhen the bill came it was over 1,600,000 dongs or USD74 or SGD 100. By Vietnamese standard , this is a very expensive dinner for two! We had lunch and dinner at many good restuarants in Vietnam and usually pay around USD$30.\n\nI suspect they know we are tourists and rip us off. Because we cannot speak Vietnamese, hard to tell them that the price is high!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten August 10, 2019",
